Sval: keep ticking a background tab's refresh driver every 10 minutes

The inactive refresh driver timer doubled its interval and, past 10
minutes, stopped scheduling until another driver joined it. A driver
with work still pending stayed attached to the stopped timer, and
EnsureTimerStarted returns early for a driver that has a timer, so it
never ticked again. Animation events are dispatched only in a tick, so
a background page that kept cancelling Web Animations queued events
without bound, each holding its animation, target and listeners. An
8-hour soak saw a YouTube tab grow about 55 MB an hour this way. This
caps the interval at 10 minutes instead, and a driver with nothing to do
still leaves the timer on its next tick.

diff --git a/layout/base/nsRefreshDriver.cpp b/layout/base/nsRefreshDriver.cpp
index 2e624b2f71..fddbfa32a6 100644
--- a/layout/base/nsRefreshDriver.cpp
+++ b/layout/base/nsRefreshDriver.cpp
@@ -111,8 +111,8 @@ static mozilla::LazyLogModule sRefreshDriverLog("nsRefreshDriver");
